1hu3|n|A minute part or portion of matter; a morsel; a little bit; an atom; a jot; as, a particle of sand, of wood, of dust. ; Any very small portion or part; the smallest portion; as, he has not a particle of patriotism or virtue. ; A crumb or little piece of concecrated host. ; The smaller hosts distributed in the communion of the laity. ; A subordinate word that is never inflected (a preposition, conjunction, interjection); or a word that can not be used except in compositions; as, ward in backward, ly in lovely.	V:1jv0,101,1;1wlx,41,1~1jv0,101,1;1wlx,41,1	N:1jv0,111,2;1jv6,97,20;1wlx,61,4~1jv6,97,20;1wlx,61,4;1jv0,111,2
