 passing; especially, one through or over some dangerous or otherwise impracticable barrier; a passageway; a defile; a ford; as, a mountain pass. ; A thrust or push; an attempt to stab or strike an adversary. ; A movement of the hand over or along anything; the manipulation of a mesmerist. ; A single passage of a bar, rail, sheet, etc., between the rolls. ; State of things; condition; predicament. ; Permission or license to pass, or to go and come; a psssport; a ticket permitting free transit or admission; as, a railroad or theater pass; a military pass. ; Fig.: a thrust; a sally of wit. ; Estimation; character. ; A part; a division.	o:1idf,46,4~1idf,46,4	d:nsc,9,2;14yr,4,8~14yr,4,8;nsc,9,2	D:2dm,11,1;1evi,5,2~1evi,5,2;2dm,11,1
